      "finalAnswer": "The route matching lives in the **`Layer` class in `lib/router/layer.js`**, with the actual regex compilation delegated to the **`path-to-regexp`** dependency.\n\n## Class: `Layer` — `lib/router/layer.js` (constructor, L33)\n\nThe regex is compiled **once, at construction time**, from the route path string:\n\n- **L16**: `var pathRegexp = require('path-to-regexp')`\n- **L45**: `this.regexp = pathRegexp(path, this.keys = [], opts)` — compiles the path (e.g. `/users/:id`) into a `RegExp` and collects parameter names into `this.keys`\n- **L48–49**: fast-path flags set on the compiled regexp: `fast_star` (path is `*`) and `fast_slash` (path is `/` with `end === false`)\n\n## Method: `Layer.prototype.match(path)` — L110–156\n\nThis is the method that tests whether the layer's path matches the incoming request URL:\n\n1. **Fast paths** (L115, L122): `fast_slash` and `fast_star` bypass the regex entirely\n2. **Core regex evaluation** (L129): `match = this.regexp.exec(path)` — the actual pattern-test against the URL path\n3. **On match** (L138–153): populates `this.params` from the captured groups (decoded via `decode_param`, L166) and sets `this.path = match[0]`; returns `true`\n4. **On no match** (L132–136): resets `this.params`/`this.path` to `undefined`, returns `false`\n\n## How it gets called\n\nThe `Router` (`lib/router/index.js`) iterates its `stack` of layers during dispatch, invoking each one through the private helper `matchLayer(layer, path)` (**L583–589**), which wraps `layer.match(path)` in a try/catch. The `path` passed in is the portion of `req.url` after any mount-path has been stripped.\n\n**In short:** `Layer` (lib/router/layer.js) holds the compiled `path-to-regexp` regex; `Layer.prototype.match` (L110) is the single method that runs `regexp.exec(url)` to decide a match and extracts route params. The regex itself is not hand-written — it comes from the external `path-to-regexp` package (declared in package.json).",
